            <ArticleTitle>Retained catheter dilator in right ventricular outflow tract for 22 years.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>679-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12180</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 61-year-old male with a retained catheter dilator in the right ventricular outflow tract for over 22 years. The management of retained intravascular foreign objects in the myocardium is reviewed.</AbstractText>
